tezgah — provenance

The commerce data model here is informed by the published design of Medusa
(github.com/medusajs/medusa), read at tag v2.18.0, which is licensed MIT
(Copyright (c) 2021 Medusajs). Copyright covers expression rather than ideas,
and no Medusa source, comment, test body, fixture or documentation text has
been copied into this repository; where the two agree it is because the same
problem has one good answer — a reservation that holds stock without
decrementing it, a payment collection that separates authorisation from
capture, one change-set mechanism serving returns, exchanges and edits alike.

Three of Medusa's architectural decisions were deliberately not taken, and the
reasons are in README.md: no foreign keys between modules, amounts stored as
a JSON `raw_` column beside a numeric one, and version rows on order items.

Medusa relicensed on 11 August 2026 to MIT with an Enterprise carve-out
covering its RBAC and SSO paths. Nothing here derives from those paths, and
they were not read.

If Medusa source is ever vendored into this repository, the MIT notice above
travels with it and this file records where.
